hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16935","He said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, and Ibn Shihab narrated, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Ibn Abbas, that he informed him that Khalid ibn al-Walid informed him that he entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon Maymuna bint al-Harith, while she was his maternal aunt. Then there was presented to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the meat of a lizard, brought by Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith from Najd, and she was under a man of Banu Jafar. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not eat anything until he knew what it was. So some of the women said: Will you not inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what he is eating? So they informed him that it was lizard meat. Then he left it. So Khalid said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Is it unlawful? He said: No, but it is food not found among my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it to me and ate it, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was looking."
"16936","Ibn Shihab said: And al-Asamm narrated to him, meaning Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, and he was in her care."
"16937","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Abdullah ibn Abbas and Khalid ibn al-Walid, that they entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the house of Maymuna. Then a roasted lizard was brought. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached for it. Then some of the women said: Inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what he intends to eat. So they said: It is a lizard, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hand. So I said: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it and ate it, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was looking."
"16938","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Alqama, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: There were words between me and Ammar ibn Yasir, so I was harsh with him in speech. Then Ammar went complaining of me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then Khalid came complaining of him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he kept being harsh with him, only increasing in harshness, while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent, not speaking. Then Ammar wept and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not see him? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his head. He said: Whoever shows enmity to Ammar, Allah will show enmity to him, and whoever hates Ammar, Allah will hate him. Khalid said: So I went out, and nothing was more beloved to me than the pleasure of Ammar. So I met him and he was pleased. Abdullah said: I heard it from my father twice."
"16939","Attab narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari informed me that Ibn Abbas informed him that Khalid ibn al-Walid, who is called the Sword of Allah, informed him that he entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon Maymuna, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while she was his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. Then he found with her a roasted lizard, brought by her sister Hufayda bint al-Harith from Najd. So the lizard was presented to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would seldom extend his hand to food until he was told of it and it was named for him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached his hand to the lizard. Then a woman among the women present said: Inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what you have presented to him. They said: It is the lizard, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hand from the lizard. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Is the lizard unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it and ate it, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was looking at me, and he did not forbid me."
"16940","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb, meaning al-Abrash, narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Sulaym Abu Salama narrated to us, from Salih, meaning Ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam, from his grandfather al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: We fought with Khalid ibn al-Walid in the summer campaign, then our companions craved meat, so they asked me and said: Will you permit us to slaughter a mare of his? So I gave it to them and they hobbled it. Then I said: Stay in your place until I come to Khalid and ask him. He said: So I came to him and asked him. Then he said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the campaign of Khaybar, then the people hastened to the enclosures of the Jews. So he ordered me to call out: Prayer is congregated, and none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim. Then he said: O people, you have hastened to the enclosures of the Jews. Verily the wealth of those under covenant is not lawful except by its right, and forbidden to you are the flesh of domestic donkeys and their horses and their mules, and every beast with a fang among predators, and every bird with a talon."
"16941","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, Baqiya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from his father, from his grandfather, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade eating the flesh of horses, mules, and donkeys."
"16942","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abu Salama al-Himsi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam, from Ibn al-Miqdam, from his grandfather al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: I fought with Khalid ibn al-Walid in the summer campaign, then my companions craved meat, so they said: Will you permit us to slaughter a mare of his? He said: So they hobbled it. So I said: Stay in your place until I come to Khalid ibn al-Walid and ask him about that. So I came to him and informed him of the news of my companions. Then he said: I fought with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the campaign of Khaybar, then the people hastened to the enclosures of the Jews. So he said: O Khalid, call out among the people that prayer is congregated, none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim. So I did. Then he stood among the people and said: O people, why have you hastened to the enclosures of the Jews. Verily the wealth of those under covenant is not lawful except by its right, and forbidden to you are domestic and tame donkeys, and their horses and their mules, and every beast with a fang among predators, and every bird with a talon."
"16943","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Azra ibn Qays, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: The Commander of the Believers wrote to me when Syria had cast its bowaniya, bathniya, and honey, and Affan once doubted, he said: When Syria cast such and such, and he ordered me to march to al-Hind, and al-Hind in our view that day was Basra. He said: While I disliked that. He said: Then a man stood and said to me: O Abu Sulayman, fear Allah, for tribulations have appeared. He said: Then he said: While Ibn al-Khattab is alive, they will only be after him. And people will be at Dhu Billiyan, and Dhu Billiyan is at such and such a place. Then a man will look and consider whether he finds a place untouched by what has befallen the place he is in of tribulation and evil, and he will not find it. He said: And those are the days which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned before the Hour, days of harj. So we seek refuge in Allah lest those days overtake us and you."
"16944","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Azra ibn Qays, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: The Commander of the Believers wrote to me when Syria had cast its bowaniya, bathniya, and honey, and Affan once doubted, he said: When Syria cast such and such, and he ordered me to march to al-Hind, and al-Hind in our view that day was Basra. He said: While I disliked that. He said: Then a man stood and said to me: O Abu Sulayman, fear Allah, for tribulations have appeared. He said: Then he said: While Ibn al-Khattab is alive, they will only be after him. And people will be at Dhu Billiyan, and Dhu Billiyan is at such and such a place. Then a man will look and consider whether he finds a place untouched by what has befallen the place he is in of tribulation and evil, and he will not find it. He said: And those are the days which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned before the Hour, days of harj. So we seek refuge in Allah lest those days overtake us and you."
"16945","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from al-Ashtar, he said: There were words between Ammar and Khalid ibn al-Walid, so Ammar complained of him to the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever shows enmity to Ammar, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will show enmity to him, and whoever hates him, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will hate him, and whoever reviles him, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will revile him. Then Salama said: This or the like."
"16946","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai and Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not take a fifth from the spoils taken from the slain."
"16947","Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab appointed Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah over Syria and dismissed Khalid ibn al-Walid. He said: Then Khalid ibn al-Walid said: There has been sent over you the trustworthy one of this umma. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The trustworthy one of this umma is Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah."
"16948","Abu Ubayda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Khalid is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and what an excellent youth of the tribe."
